{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Application Layer.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Application Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"application layer application layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Application Layer.md","fileName":"Application Layer.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Application Layer","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-22 20:53\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Application Commands and Service Boundaries]] [[OSI Layers Packets and Network Streams]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Application Commands and Service Boundaries","OSI Layers Packets and Network Streams","Domain Model","Public API Contract","Entity Invariant","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf","hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Application Layer.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Application Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"application layer application layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Application Layer.md","fileName":"Application Layer.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Application Layer","heading":"Application Layer","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The application layer coordinates a use case around an isolated [[Domain Model]]. It receives a [[Public API Contract]] or message, obtains the required aggregate or services, invokes domain behavior, and persists the resulting changes. It can implement infrastructure-facing interfaces declared by the domain, but it should not reimplement [[Entity Invariant]]s. The layer is an outer boundary: it translates between delivery mechanisms and the domain while keeping business decisions in domain objects.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Application Commands and Service Boundaries","OSI Layers Packets and Network Streams","Domain Model","Public API Cont